      ("p", "A repair goes through several stages, and not all of them are visible from outside. Some days the car seems idle when in fact it's waiting for a part or for the [[perito|loss adjuster]] to visit. That's why we keep you informed in real time of the status of the repair: you know what stage your car is at without having to call."),
      ("h2", "The usual stages of a repair"),
      ("checks", [
        "Vehicle check-in and signing of the [[orden-de-reparacion|repair order]].",
        "Diagnosis or damage assessment and preparation of the estimate.",
        "Your approval or, for insurance jobs, [[peritacion|loss assessment]] and authorisation from the insurer.",
        "Ordering and receiving parts.",
        "Repair: mechanical, bodywork, preparation and paint, as needed.",
        "Reassembly, quality check, cleaning and notice that it's ready.",
      ]),
      ("h2", "When something unexpected comes up"),
      ("p", "Sometimes, when a part is removed, hidden damage appears: a broken bracket behind a bumper or a worn component. If that happens, we don't carry on regardless. We tell you, explain the options and, if needed, extend the [estimate](servicio-presupuesto-sin-compromiso.html) for your approval. On insurance jobs, we also inform the insurer."),
      ("h2", "Timescales: what depends on us and what doesn't"),
